CODEGEN.md §2.8, §4.4, DECISIONS 438 (ADR-0026 §10.2): a constant of another package's variant kind names that package's kind enum, so a's ts emit needs b to have a ts emit (E8004), as for any reference to b's type; the IR keeps the variant of a kind's type.
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// A reward.
variant Reward {
  /// Gold.
  gold
  /// An item.
  item {
    /// How many.
    count: Int
  }
}

emit go { out: "@features/b" }
-- a/a.canon --
package a

import b { Reward }

/// The kind of gold.
const K = Reward.gold.kind

emit ts { out: "@features/a/a.ts" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8004]  a/a.canon:8:6
  b.Reward of package b is used by this ts emit, but b has no ts emit

1 error, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
